<title>BELGIUM: Belgian yr/yr inflation 2.46 pct in October.</title>
<headline>Belgian yr/yr inflation 2.46 pct in October.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian Economic Affairs Ministry released the following data on inflation -</p>
<p>    BELGIAN CONSUMER PRICES     October    September  Oct 1995</p>
<p>    Index (base 100=1988)	 123.38     123.02     120.42</p>
<p>    Mth/mth change (in pct)	 0.29	-0.20	-0.18</p>
<p>    Yr/yr change (in pct)	   2.46	 1.97	 1.22</p>
<p>    Health index *		  121.00     120.81</p>
<p>    Mth/mth change (in pct)	 0.16	 0.30</p>
<p>NOTE - * excludes products such as tobacco, alcohol and petrol, is used for inflation adjustments of rents and wages.</p>
<p>The ministry said price rises were mainly seen for liquid fuels, car fuel, fresh fruit and diesel, while prices for fresh vegetables, flowers and plants and potatoes were lower.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
